---
title: Beef Rouladen
servings: 6
cookTime: 3.5 hours
rating: 5
description: Dorf Haus Supper Club, Sauk City, WI
source.name: Wisconsin Supper Club Cookbook
tags: Alcohol, Beef
---

Preheat oven to 350°F. 

Place @Sirloin steaks{6}(1/4" thick, 8oz each) on a flat surface and spread a thin layer of @mustard{6%tablespoons}(med hot German mustard) on each one. 
Season with @salt and pepper{}(to taste).

Place one @dill pickle wedges{6} at one end of each steak. 
Place two @strips bacon{12} near the center of each steak. 
Cover bacon strips with @thin sliced onions{2}.

Starting at the pickle end, tightly roll steaks. 
Do not push out bacon or onion slices. 
Place rolled meat into a #baking pan{} that is at least 4 inches deep. 

Add @white wine{3/4%cup}(boiled) to pan.
Combine @mushrooms{12%ounces}(sliced) and @brown gravy{4%cups} in a bowl, and pour over beef rolls.

Cover and cook ~{3 - 3.5%hours}, or until meat is tender.
